                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.44A15/141: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Des Portes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-07T12:00:00-06:00">March 7,
                        1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. My telegram No. 24, March 5, 1 p.m. It is my considered opinion that unless
                    the British Government is willing to enlarge the terms of reference there is
                    grave danger of an immediate breakdown in the negotiations. Please forward this
                    opinion to Mr. Welles. The British Minister is of the same opinion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Des Portes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
